{
  "dom_id": "step-q47137",
  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "A randomly selected group of students from a high school were asked about their favorite sport between baseball, football, basketball, or soccer. The results of the survey are summarized in the two-way frequency table below.\n\n|  | Baseball | Football | Basketball | Soccer | Totals |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Girls | $10$ | $19$ | $10$ | $12$ | $51$ |\n| Boys | $10$ | $13$ | $20$ | $6$ | $49$ |\n| Totals | $20$ | $32$ | $30$ | $18$ | $100$ |\n\nLet $F$ be the event that a randomly selected student in the high school is a **\"Girl\"** whose favorite sport is **\"Football\"**, and $S$ be the event that a randomly selected student in the high school is a **\"Girl\"** whose favorite sport is **\"Soccer\"**. Estimate $P(F\\cup S).$",
